    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded an email-uniqueness check to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, mirroring the existing telephone/household duplicate-rule pattern so each concern stays in its own small class:\n\n1. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerEmail`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 reads the already-normalized (lower-cased) body variable, skips when no email is supplied (email stays optional), and throws `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` if any existing owner uses the same lower-cased email. It reuses `OwnerEmail.normalize` to canonicalize stored emails for comparison rather than duplicating that logic.\n\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception carrying the offending email.\n\n3. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail`, built via the shared `ProblemDetails.build` helper.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `...DuplicateOwnerEmailException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted a `uniqueEmail` step (governed by the same transaction) into `owners.POST.yml`, right after the telephone check and before any entity is built or persisted.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
